concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45ah a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45AH Determining guilt"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-45ah ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG even if:  (a) each other party to the contract, arrangement or understanding is a person who is not criminally responsible; or  (b) subject to subsection (2), all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of the offence. Note: Party has an extended meaning—see section 45AC.  (2) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  Schedule 1  The Schedule version of Part IV" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG even if:  (a) each other party to the contract, arrangement or understanding is a person who is not criminally responsible; or  (b) subject to subsection (2), all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of the offence. Note: Party has an extended meaning—see section 45AC.  (2) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  Schedule 1  The Schedule version of Part IV"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "074e8ae5b989ffd5f577be0d9b930e5c8079784a9a2c8417daad4ee49c351b6b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
