doc:sch-1-sec-45d-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45D(2) Secondary boycotts for the purpose of causing substantial loss" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes that include that purpose.  The Schedule version of Part IV  Schedule 1 Schedule version of Part IV  Part 1 Other provisions  Division 2  Section 45DA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45da a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45DA Secondary boycotts for the purpose of causing substantial"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-45da ;
    values:originalText "lessening of competition  (1) A person must not, in concert with a second person, engage in conduct:  (a) that hinders or prevents:  (i) a third person supplying goods or services to a fourth person (who is not an employer of the first person or the second person); or  (ii) a third person acquiring goods or services from a fourth person (who is not an employer of the first person or the second person); and  (b) that is engaged in for the purpose, and would have or be likely to have the effect, of causing a substantial lessening of competition in any market in which the fourth person supplies or acquires goods or services. Note 1: Conduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be authorised under section 88. Note 2: This section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with permitted boycotts.  (2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes that include that purpose. Note: This version of Part IV does not contain an equivalent of section 45DB of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010." ;
    skos:definition "lessening of competition  (1) A person must not, in concert with a second person, engage in conduct:  (a) that hinders or prevents:  (i) a third person supplying goods or services to a fourth person (who is not an employer of the first person or the second person); or  (ii) a third person acquiring goods or services from a fourth person (who is not an employer of the first person or the second person); and  (b) that is engaged in for the purpose, and would have or be likely to have the effect, of causing a substantial lessening of competition in any market in which the fourth person supplies or acquires goods or services. Note 1: Conduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be authorised under section 88. Note 2: This section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with permitted boycotts.  (2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes that include that purpose. Note: This version of Part IV does not contain an equivalent of section 45DB of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5c9a5cdff7f0f91fe04aa6390a9c7da15f4ed0db2e870017ea2fd535c499e2ea" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45da-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45da-ss-2 ;
