doc:sch-2-sec-3-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3(1) Meaning of consumer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person is taken to have acquired particular goods as a consumer if, and only if:  (a) the amount paid or payable for the goods, as worked out under subsections (4) to (9), did not exceed:  (i) $40,000; or  (ii) if a greater amount is prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph—that greater amount; or  (b) the goods were of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 1  Introduction  Section 3  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) the goods consisted of a vehicle or trailer acquired for use principally in the transport of goods on public roads." ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer .

