concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-3-ss-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3(11) Meaning of consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-3-ss-11 ;
    values:originalText "(11) A purchase or other acquisition of goods or services is made by a mixed supply if the goods or services are purchased or acquired together with other property or services, or together with both other property and other services.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Introduction  Chapter 1  Section 4  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Supplies to consumers" ;
    skos:definition "(11) A purchase or other acquisition of goods or services is made by a mixed supply if the goods or services are purchased or acquired together with other property or services, or together with both other property and other services.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Introduction  Chapter 1  Section 4  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Supplies to consumers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "69e0e1627368f96b6e2074c204b4c412bef64400184f814740d8b470786d31ef" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-3 ;
