doc:sch-2-sec-4-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(1) Misleading representations with respect to future matters" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person makes a representation with respect to any future matter (including the doing of, or the refusing to do, any act); and  (b) the person does not have reasonable grounds for making the representation; the representation is taken, for the purposes of this Schedule, to be misleading." ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-4-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(2) Misleading representations with respect to future matters"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-4-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to a proceeding concerning a representation made with respect to a future matter by:  (a) a party to the proceeding; or  (b) any other person; the party or other person is taken not to have had reasonable grounds for making the representation, unless evidence is adduced to the contrary." ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to a proceeding concerning a representation made with respect to a future matter by:  (a) a party to the proceeding; or  (b) any other person; the party or other person is taken not to have had reasonable grounds for making the representation, unless evidence is adduced to the contrary."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ff831022bbafbf5868e60497f987f2e8e84c593d8f0262e4c53c3102488ea42b" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-4 ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Treats donations of goods or services as supplies and acquisitions. Party or other person is not deemed to have had reasonable grounds for making a representation unless evidence is adduced to the contrary." ;
