    values:originalText "(4) An inference that goods have a safety defect is not to be made only because:  (a) there was compliance with a Commonwealth mandatory standard for them; and  (b) that standard was not the safest possible standard having regard to the latest state of scientific or technical knowledge when they were supplied by their manufacturer.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Introduction  Chapter 1  Section 10  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(4) An inference that goods have a safety defect is not to be made only because:  (a) there was compliance with a Commonwealth mandatory standard for them; and  (b) that standard was not the safest possible standard having regard to the latest state of scientific or technical knowledge when they were supplied by their manufacturer.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Introduction  Chapter 1  Section 10  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ff115bd6ea6b992332d52ff3505bbb4a8f7b76b7aad52265dc08aa507a57d42a" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-9 ;
    cof:pageNumber "114"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Goods have a safety defect if there is an inference based on non-compliance with the safest possible standard." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
