    cml:premiseText "(4) An inference that goods have a safety defect is not to be made only because:  (a) there was compliance with a Commonwealth mandatory standard for them; and  (b) that standard was not the safest possible standard having regard to the latest state of scientific or technical knowledge when they were supplied by their manufacturer." ;
