concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Unconscionable conduct within the meaning of the unwritten law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, engage in conduct that is unconscionable, within the meaning of the unwritten law from time to time. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) This section does not apply to conduct that is prohibited by section 21." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, engage in conduct that is unconscionable, within the meaning of the unwritten law from time to time. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) This section does not apply to conduct that is prohibited by section 21."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6035263dc1c9e899161decd2beb8ceec635a72cf0a7aa4454bf6033941704ee6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "123"^^xsd:integer ;
