concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23-ss-2c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23(2C) Unfair terms of consumer contracts and small business contracts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23-ss-2c ;
    values:originalText "(2C) A person contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the person applies or relies on, or purports to apply or rely on, a term of a contract; and  (b) the contract is a consumer contract or small business contract; and  (c) the contract is a standard form contract; and  (d) the term is unfair. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection: see section 224." ;
    skos:definition "(2C) A person contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the person applies or relies on, or purports to apply or rely on, a term of a contract; and  (b) the contract is a consumer contract or small business contract; and  (c) the contract is a standard form contract; and  (d) the term is unfair. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection: see section 224."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "490f80facd2b6d3c335967adcf082effe93339962c04bad7eb7e1ed93d2d830a" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23 ;
