doc:sch-2-sec-23-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23(3) Unfair terms of consumer contracts and small business contracts" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A consumer contract is a contract for:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 General protections  Chapter 2 Unfair contract terms  Part 2-3  Section 23  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) a supply of goods or services; or  (b) a sale or grant of an interest in land; to an individual whose acquisition of the goods, services or interest is wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use or consumption." ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23(4) Unfair terms of consumer contracts and small business contracts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) A contract is a small business contract if:  (a) the contract is for a supply of goods or services, or a sale or grant of an interest in land; and  (b) at least one party to the contract satisfies either or both of the following conditions:  (i) the party makes the contract in the course of carrying on a business and at a time when the party employs fewer than 100 persons;  (ii) the party’s turnover, worked out under subsection (6) for the party’s last income year (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) that ended at or before the time when the contract is made, is less than $10,000,000." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A contract is a small business contract if:  (a) the contract is for a supply of goods or services, or a sale or grant of an interest in land; and  (b) at least one party to the contract satisfies either or both of the following conditions:  (i) the party makes the contract in the course of carrying on a business and at a time when the party employs fewer than 100 persons;  (ii) the party’s turnover, worked out under subsection (6) for the party’s last income year (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) that ended at or before the time when the contract is made, is less than $10,000,000."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cbca8a5985e95f726630b030d55c7a9a21d6c06e8ae6d7daa6fc44b1fda9eb54" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23 ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Contract is a small business contract if certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.128" ;
