    skos:definition "(2) The upfront price payable under a contract is the consideration that:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 General protections  Chapter 2 Unfair contract terms  Part 2-3  Section 27  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) is provided, or is to be provided, for the supply, sale or grant under the contract; and  (b) is disclosed at or before the time the contract is entered into; but does not include any other consideration that is contingent on the occurrence or non-occurrence of a particular event."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1d7925900e3599ad56cbb986168823cfbffc13920eeb59ffaafe858a77f42253" ;
