    values:originalText "(3) However, subsection (2) does not apply to or in relation to unsolicited goods sent to a person if:  (a) the person has, at any time during the recovery period, unreasonably refused to permit the sender or the owner of the goods to take possession of the goods; or  (b) the sender or the owner of the goods has within the recovery period taken possession of the goods; or  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Unfair practices  Part 3-1  Section 42  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) the goods were received by the person in circumstances in which the person knew, or might reasonably be expected to have known, that the goods were not intended for him or her." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, subsection (2) does not apply to or in relation to unsolicited goods sent to a person if:  (a) the person has, at any time during the recovery period, unreasonably refused to permit the sender or the owner of the goods to take possession of the goods; or  (b) the sender or the owner of the goods has within the recovery period taken possession of the goods; or  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Unfair practices  Part 3-1  Section 42  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) the goods were received by the person in circumstances in which the person knew, or might reasonably be expected to have known, that the goods were not intended for him or her."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fccaf6f9534a88fa7aa7d409ff1bbbee2de1ce1cf0a42c3ecb00f87aff3cee41" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-41 ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemption from liability for unsolicited goods under certain circumstances." ;
