doc:sch-2-sec-56 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56 Guarantee relating to the supply of goods by description" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods by description to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods correspond with the description.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    cof:pageNumber "165"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-57 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57 Guarantees relating to the supply of goods by sample or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-57 ;
    values:originalText "demonstration model  (1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer by reference to a sample or demonstration model; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that:  (c) the goods correspond with the sample or demonstration model in quality, state or condition; and  (d) if the goods are supplied by reference to a sample—the consumer will have a reasonable opportunity to compare the goods with the sample; and  (e) the goods are free from any defect that:  (i) would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample or demonstration model; and  (ii) would cause the goods not to be of acceptable quality.  (2) If goods are supplied by reference to a sample or demonstration model as well as by description, the guarantees in section 56 and in this section both apply." ;
    skos:definition "demonstration model  (1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer by reference to a sample or demonstration model; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that:  (c) the goods correspond with the sample or demonstration model in quality, state or condition; and  (d) if the goods are supplied by reference to a sample—the consumer will have a reasonable opportunity to compare the goods with the sample; and  (e) the goods are free from any defect that:  (i) would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample or demonstration model; and  (ii) would cause the goods not to be of acceptable quality.  (2) If goods are supplied by reference to a sample or demonstration model as well as by description, the guarantees in section 56 and in this section both apply."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d6656bde8f04d48a93a0ae6c2d80ed911a6c34cd0a4b55b86d726ebf898a8ced" ;
    cof:pageNumber "166"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-57-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-57-ss-2 ;
