concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-59 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59 Guarantee as to express warranties"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-59 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will comply with any express warranty given or made by the manufacturer in relation to the goods.  (2) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the supplier will comply with any express warranty given or made by the supplier in relation to the goods.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will comply with any express warranty given or made by the manufacturer in relation to the goods.  (2) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the supplier will comply with any express warranty given or made by the supplier in relation to the goods.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections"@en ;
