doc:sch-2-sec-66-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "66(1) Display notices" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commonwealth Minister may determine, in writing, that persons (the suppliers) who make supplies, or supplies of a specified kind, to which guarantees apply under this Division are required to display, in accordance with the determination, a notice that meets the requirements of the determination." ;
    cof:pageNumber "172"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-66-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66(2) Display notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-66-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A supplier who makes a supply to a consumer to which a guarantee applies under this Division, and to which such a determination relates, must ensure that a notice that meets those requirements is, in accordance with the determination:  (a) if the consumer takes delivery of the goods or services at the supplier’s premises—displayed at those premises; or  (b) otherwise—drawn to the consumer’s attention before the consumer agrees to the supply of the goods. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A supplier who makes a supply to a consumer to which a guarantee applies under this Division, and to which such a determination relates, must ensure that a notice that meets those requirements is, in accordance with the determination:  (a) if the consumer takes delivery of the goods or services at the supplier’s premises—displayed at those premises; or  (b) otherwise—drawn to the consumer’s attention before the consumer agrees to the supply of the goods. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a692a4c487c85cb639c41c957de7035ea8735166ae49bc7645de8813abae1841" ;
