doc:sch-2-sec-69-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "69(4) Meaning of unsolicited consumer agreement" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) However, despite subsections (1) and (3), an agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are not unsolicited consumer agreements." ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-70 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "70 Presumption that agreements are unsolicited consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-70 ;
    values:originalText "agreements  (1) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), an agreement is presumed to be an unsolicited consumer agreement if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement.  (2) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), it is presumed that a proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made if:  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    skos:definition "agreements  (1) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), an agreement is presumed to be an unsolicited consumer agreement if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement.  (2) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), it is presumed that a proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made if:  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bbf2df780dbc780dcd702a1bb88cde7d6f686789b6249d88ad67e102a6d185f6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-70-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-70-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.175" .
doc:sch-2-sec-70 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "70 Presumption that agreements are unsolicited consumer" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "agreements  (1) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), an agreement is presumed to be an unsolicited consumer agreement if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement.  (2) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), it is presumed that a proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made if:  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer .

