doc:sch-2-sec-84 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "84 Obligations of suppliers on termination" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the supplier under the agreement must, immediately upon being notified of the termination, return or refund to the consumer under the agreement any consideration (or the value of any consideration) that the consumer gave under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-85 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85 Obligations and rights of consumers on termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-85 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the consumer under the agreement must, within a reasonable time:  (a) return to the supplier under the agreement any goods:  (i) that have been received from the supplier under the agreement; and  (ii) that the consumer has not already consumed; or  (b) notify the supplier of the place where the supplier may collect the goods.  (2) The goods become the property of the consumer, freed and discharged from all liens and charges of any description, if:  (a) the consumer gives notice to the supplier under subsection (1)(b); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the consumer under the agreement must, within a reasonable time:  (a) return to the supplier under the agreement any goods:  (i) that have been received from the supplier under the agreement; and  (ii) that the consumer has not already consumed; or  (b) notify the supplier of the place where the supplier may collect the goods.  (2) The goods become the property of the consumer, freed and discharged from all liens and charges of any description, if:  (a) the consumer gives notice to the supplier under subsection (1)(b); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0a1e55b0d17c7e2136ba76500cd1e1e55a8bd9b5db42a14b6f2e4a01d34f702e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer ;
