concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-97 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "97 Termination of lay-by agreements by consumers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-97 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A consumer who is party to a lay-by agreement may terminate the agreement at any time before the goods to which the agreement relates are delivered to the consumer under the agreement.  (2) A supplier of goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that the agreement does not require the consumer to pay a  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Consumer transactions  Part 3-2  Section 98  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  charge (a termination charge) for the termination of the agreement unless:  (a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A supplier of goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that, if the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable, the amount of the charge is not more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A consumer who is party to a lay-by agreement may terminate the agreement at any time before the goods to which the agreement relates are delivered to the consumer under the agreement.  (2) A supplier of goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that the agreement does not require the consumer to pay a  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Consumer transactions  Part 3-2  Section 98  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  charge (a termination charge) for the termination of the agreement unless:  (a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A supplier of goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that, if the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable, the amount of the charge is not more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "230ce047ee90b00b82af4eca66b019648095c3290971c9f65074197c1878e632" ;
    cof:pageNumber "192"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-97-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-97-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-97-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
