doc:sch-2-sec-98 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "98 Termination of lay-by agreements by suppliers" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A supplier of goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must not terminate the agreement unless:  (a) the consumer who is a party to the agreement breached a term of the agreement; or  (b) the supplier is no longer engaged in trade or commerce; or  (c) the goods to which the agreement relates are no longer available. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "193"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-99 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "99 Effect of termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-99 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a lay-by agreement is terminated by a party to the agreement, the supplier must refund to the consumer all the amounts paid by the consumer under the agreement other than any termination charge that is payable under the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) The supplier is entitled to recover any unpaid termination charge from the consumer as a debt if the amounts paid by the consumer under the lay-by agreement are not enough to cover the charge.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a lay-by agreement is terminated by a party to the agreement, the supplier must refund to the consumer all the amounts paid by the consumer under the agreement other than any termination charge that is payable under the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) The supplier is entitled to recover any unpaid termination charge from the consumer as a debt if the amounts paid by the consumer under the lay-by agreement are not enough to cover the charge.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3299ef4c08e77a62cd82ea2115fddcca7d981b35b7f9c218565afb729deb0ade" ;
    cof:pageNumber "193"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-99-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-99-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.193" .
doc:sch-2-sec-99 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "99 Effect of termination" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a lay-by agreement is terminated by a party to the agreement, the supplier must refund to the consumer all the amounts paid by the consumer under the agreement other than any termination charge that is payable under the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) The supplier is entitled to recover any unpaid termination charge from the consumer as a debt if the amounts paid by the consumer under the lay-by agreement are not enough to cover the charge.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    cof:pageNumber "193"^^xsd:integer .

