concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-101 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "101 Consumer may request an itemised bill"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-101 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a person (the supplier), in trade or commerce, supplies services to a consumer, the consumer may request that the supplier give the consumer an itemised bill that:  (a) specifies how the price of the services was calculated; and  (b) includes, if applicable, the number of hours of labour that related to the supply of the services and the hourly rate for that labour; and  (c) includes, if applicable, a list of the materials used to supply the services and the amount charged for those materials.  (2) The request under subsection (1) must be made within 30 days after:  (a) the services are supplied; or  (b) the consumer receives a bill or account from the supplier for the supply of the services; whichever occurs later.  (3) The supplier must give the consumer the itemised bill within 7 days after the request is made. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (4) The supplier must not charge the consumer for the itemised bill.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Consumer transactions  Part 3-2  Section 102  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (5) The supplier must ensure that the itemised bill is transparent." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a person (the supplier), in trade or commerce, supplies services to a consumer, the consumer may request that the supplier give the consumer an itemised bill that:  (a) specifies how the price of the services was calculated; and  (b) includes, if applicable, the number of hours of labour that related to the supply of the services and the hourly rate for that labour; and  (c) includes, if applicable, a list of the materials used to supply the services and the amount charged for those materials.  (2) The request under subsection (1) must be made within 30 days after:  (a) the services are supplied; or  (b) the consumer receives a bill or account from the supplier for the supply of the services; whichever occurs later.  (3) The supplier must give the consumer the itemised bill within 7 days after the request is made. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (4) The supplier must not charge the consumer for the itemised bill.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Consumer transactions  Part 3-2  Section 102  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (5) The supplier must ensure that the itemised bill is transparent."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b023be415db1411ffda62611a56799ff1a74b1afe45b331b0bd5a8b73c67eb26" ;
