concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102 Prescribed requirements for warranties against defects"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-102 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulations may prescribe requirements relating to the form and content of warranties against defects.  (2) A person must not, in connection with the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or services to a consumer:  (a) give to the consumer a document that evidences a warranty against defects that does not comply with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of subsection (1); or  (b) represent directly to the consumer that the goods or services are goods or services to which such a warranty against defects relates. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A warranty against defects is a representation communicated to a consumer in connection with the supply of goods or services, at or about the time of supply, to the effect that a person will (unconditionally or on specified conditions):  (a) repair or replace the goods or part of them; or  (b) provide again or rectify the services or part of them; or  (c) wholly or partly recompense the consumer; if the goods or services or part of them are defective, and includes any document by which such a representation is evidenced." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulations may prescribe requirements relating to the form and content of warranties against defects.  (2) A person must not, in connection with the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or services to a consumer:  (a) give to the consumer a document that evidences a warranty against defects that does not comply with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of subsection (1); or  (b) represent directly to the consumer that the goods or services are goods or services to which such a warranty against defects relates. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A warranty against defects is a representation communicated to a consumer in connection with the supply of goods or services, at or about the time of supply, to the effect that a person will (unconditionally or on specified conditions):  (a) repair or replace the goods or part of them; or  (b) provide again or rectify the services or part of them; or  (c) wholly or partly recompense the consumer; if the goods or services or part of them are defective, and includes any document by which such a representation is evidenced."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "39e9624b7f1488d131d02945c96d09425cb63e77001045f9a2edc960a8a6eb58" ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
