doc:sch-2-sec-102-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "102(2) Prescribed requirements for warranties against defects" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person must not, in connection with the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or services to a consumer:  (a) give to the consumer a document that evidences a warranty against defects that does not comply with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of subsection (1); or  (b) represent directly to the consumer that the goods or services are goods or services to which such a warranty against defects relates. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection." ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102(3) Prescribed requirements for warranties against defects"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-102-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A warranty against defects is a representation communicated to a consumer in connection with the supply of goods or services, at or about the time of supply, to the effect that a person will (unconditionally or on specified conditions):  (a) repair or replace the goods or part of them; or  (b) provide again or rectify the services or part of them; or  (c) wholly or partly recompense the consumer; if the goods or services or part of them are defective, and includes any document by which such a representation is evidenced." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A warranty against defects is a representation communicated to a consumer in connection with the supply of goods or services, at or about the time of supply, to the effect that a person will (unconditionally or on specified conditions):  (a) repair or replace the goods or part of them; or  (b) provide again or rectify the services or part of them; or  (c) wholly or partly recompense the consumer; if the goods or services or part of them are defective, and includes any document by which such a representation is evidenced."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "da2acb2d2e584731411207810ab47fcd73c97d7565ce3f033821acde4c51a626" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102 ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Warranty against defects must be unconditional or on specified conditions." ;
    dc:description "Repair, replace, provide again, rectify, or recompense the consumer if goods/services are defective." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.201" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-102-ss-3-norm .
