    skos:definition "(1) A responsible Minister may, by written notice published on the internet, impose an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind if:  (a) it appears to the responsible Minister that:  (i) consumer goods of that kind will or may cause injury to any person; or  (ii) a reasonably foreseeable use (including a misuse) of consumer goods of that kind will or may cause injury to any person; or  (b) another responsible Minister has imposed, under paragraph (a), an interim ban:  (i) on consumer goods of the same kind; or  (ii) on consumer goods of a kind that includes those goods;  and that ban is still in force."@en ;
