concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-121 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "121 Temporary exemption under the Mutual Recognition Act 1992"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-121 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 3-3  Section 121  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind is in force; and  (b) the interim ban was not imposed by the Commonwealth Minister; the goods are taken, for the purposes of section 15 of the Mutual Recognition Act 1992, to be goods of a kind that are declared, in the manner provided by section 15(1) of that Act, to be goods to which that section applies.  (2) This section does not affect the application of section 15(3) of that Act in relation to such an exemption.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 3-3  Section 121  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind is in force; and  (b) the interim ban was not imposed by the Commonwealth Minister; the goods are taken, for the purposes of section 15 of the Mutual Recognition Act 1992, to be goods of a kind that are declared, in the manner provided by section 15(1) of that Act, to be goods to which that section applies.  (2) This section does not affect the application of section 15(3) of that Act in relation to such an exemption.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 3  Specific protections"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "57b3b4e30246151631376c4bdfc6b81d0af0e4f1d3f38f4184a90cde46470334" ;
    cof:pageNumber "216"^^xsd:integer ;
