concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-124-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "124(4) Obligations of a supplier in relation to a recall notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-124-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the supplier undertakes:  (a) to repair the consumer goods; or  (b) to replace the consumer goods; the cost of the repair or replacement, including any necessary transportation costs, must be paid by the supplier.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 3-3  Section 125  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the supplier undertakes:  (a) to repair the consumer goods; or  (b) to replace the consumer goods; the cost of the repair or replacement, including any necessary transportation costs, must be paid by the supplier.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Specific protections  Chapter 3 Safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 3-3  Section 125  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "54c9cca736b4df4b0690d3c6cd9820aebbeb7c4aaa39b2ce3d9fbdf6e7f52da9" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-124 ;
    cof:pageNumber "220"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplier must pay for repair or replacement of consumer goods." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.220" ;
