concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-155 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "155 Misleading conduct as to the nature etc. of goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-155 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in trade or commerce, engages in conduct that is liable to mislead the public as to the nature, the manufacturing process, the characteristics, the suitability for their purpose or the quantity of any goods.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in trade or commerce, engages in conduct that is liable to mislead the public as to the nature, the manufacturing process, the characteristics, the suitability for their purpose or the quantity of any goods.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "594cc44d46fbb4b224ecf4bbc7986fd7030bca398bd77f2e7ba17aaf91fda873" ;
    cof:pageNumber "253"^^xsd:integer ;
