concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-174-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "174(1) Requirement to give document to the consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-174-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the agreement, or (if the agreement was negotiated by telephone) the agreement document, does not comply with the following requirements:  (a) it must set out in full all the terms of the agreement, including:  (i) the total consideration to be paid or provided by the consumer under the agreement or, if the total consideration is not ascertainable at the time the agreement is made, the way in which it is to be calculated; and  (ii) any postal or delivery charges to be paid by the consumer;  (b) its front page must include a notice that:  (i) conspicuously and prominently informs the consumer of the consumer’s right to terminate the agreement; and  (ii) conspicuously and prominently sets out any other information prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of section 79(b)(ii); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the agreement, or (if the agreement was negotiated by telephone) the agreement document, does not comply with the following requirements:  (a) it must set out in full all the terms of the agreement, including:  (i) the total consideration to be paid or provided by the consumer under the agreement or, if the total consideration is not ascertainable at the time the agreement is made, the way in which it is to be calculated; and  (ii) any postal or delivery charges to be paid by the consumer;  (b) its front page must include a notice that:  (i) conspicuously and prominently informs the consumer of the consumer’s right to terminate the agreement; and  (ii) conspicuously and prominently sets out any other information prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of section 79(b)(ii); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cec08a194ba0465a78565e4948d51141d0637e395591ac8e658d8d27e3cbee16" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-174 ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplier must comply with specific requirements in unsolicited consumer agreements. Dealer must give consumer a copy of the agreement immediately after signing." ;
    dc:description "The agreement document must set out all terms, including total consideration and postal charges." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.278" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-174-ss-1-norm .
