doc:sch-2-sec-174-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "174(1) Requirement to give document to the consumer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the agreement, or (if the agreement was negotiated by telephone) the agreement document, does not comply with the following requirements:  (a) it must set out in full all the terms of the agreement, including:  (i) the total consideration to be paid or provided by the consumer under the agreement or, if the total consideration is not ascertainable at the time the agreement is made, the way in which it is to be calculated; and  (ii) any postal or delivery charges to be paid by the consumer;  (b) its front page must include a notice that:  (i) conspicuously and prominently informs the consumer of the consumer’s right to terminate the agreement; and  (ii) conspicuously and prominently sets out any other information prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of section 79(b)(ii); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences" ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-176 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "176 Additional requirements for unsolicited consumer agreements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-176 ;
    values:originalText "not negotiated by telephone  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement that was not negotiated by telephone commits an offence if the agreement does not comply with the following requirements:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to consumer transactions  Part 4-2  Section 177  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the agreement must be signed by the consumer under the agreement;  (b) if the agreement is signed by a person on the supplier’s behalf—the agreement must state that the person is acting on the supplier’s behalf, and must set out in full:  (i) the person’s name; and  (ii) the person’s business address (not being a post box) or, if the person does not have a business address, the person’s residential address; and  (iii) if the person has an email address—the person’s email address. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  (3) This section does not limit the operation of section 175." ;
    skos:definition "not negotiated by telephone  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement that was not negotiated by telephone commits an offence if the agreement does not comply with the following requirements:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to consumer transactions  Part 4-2  Section 177  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the agreement must be signed by the consumer under the agreement;  (b) if the agreement is signed by a person on the supplier’s behalf—the agreement must state that the person is acting on the supplier’s behalf, and must set out in full:  (i) the person’s name; and  (ii) the person’s business address (not being a post box) or, if the person does not have a business address, the person’s residential address; and  (iii) if the person has an email address—the person’s email address. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  (3) This section does not limit the operation of section 175."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4c32f2b89fc830d38024601b299eb33722789988709591aee367a49ccb5ecc52" ;
    cof:pageNumber "280"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-176-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-176-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-176-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.280" .
doc:sch-2-sec-176 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "176 Additional requirements for unsolicited consumer agreements" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "not negotiated by telephone  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement that was not negotiated by telephone commits an offence if the agreement does not comply with the following requirements:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to consumer transactions  Part 4-2  Section 177  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the agreement must be signed by the consumer under the agreement;  (b) if the agreement is signed by a person on the supplier’s behalf—the agreement must state that the person is acting on the supplier’s behalf, and must set out in full:  (i) the person’s name; and  (ii) the person’s business address (not being a post box) or, if the person does not have a business address, the person’s residential address; and  (iii) if the person has an email address—the person’s email address. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  (3) This section does not limit the operation of section 175." ;
    cof:pageNumber "280"^^xsd:integer .

