concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-177 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "177 Requirements for amendments of unsolicited consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-177 ;
    values:originalText "agreements  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if any amendments to the agreement are not signed by both parties to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences" ;
    skos:definition "agreements  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if any amendments to the agreement are not signed by both parties to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bbf2df780dbc780dcd702a1bb88cde7d6f686789b6249d88ad67e102a6d185f6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "281"^^xsd:integer ;
