concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-180 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180 Repayment of payments received after termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-180 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82; and  (b) the supplier does not immediately refund to the consumer under the agreement any payment:  (i) that the consumer, or a person acting on the consumer’s behalf, makes to the supplier after the termination; and  (ii) that purports to be made under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82; and  (b) the supplier does not immediately refund to the consumer under the agreement any payment:  (i) that the consumer, or a person acting on the consumer’s behalf, makes to the supplier after the termination; and  (ii) that purports to be made under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "94e0130c27f14f7410c64ee85444bd30218409fbb0236b29aca712c6dc35988f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "283"^^xsd:integer ;
