concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-187 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187 Application of this Division to certain conduct covered by the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-187 ;
    values:originalText "Corporations Act  This Division does not apply in relation to conduct to which section 992A of the Corporations Act 2001 applies. Note: Section 992A of the Corporations Act 2001 prohibits hawking of financial products.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to consumer transactions  Part 4-2  Section 188  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "Corporations Act  This Division does not apply in relation to conduct to which section 992A of the Corporations Act 2001 applies. Note: Section 992A of the Corporations Act 2001 prohibits hawking of financial products.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to consumer transactions  Part 4-2  Section 188  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7c05ea27574f6d7fa276ff28237a0a4677407edbbf7fc02691d90b4859bda2a8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "286"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Section 992A of the Corporations Act 2001 prohibits hawking of financial products." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
