concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-192 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "192 Prescribed requirements for warranties against defects"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-192 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in connection with the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or services to a consumer:  (a) gives to the consumer a document that evidences a warranty against defects and that does not comply with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of section 102(1); or  (b) represents directly to the consumer that the goods or services are goods or services to which such a warranty against defects relates. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in connection with the supply, in trade or commerce, of goods or services to a consumer:  (a) gives to the consumer a document that evidences a warranty against defects and that does not comply with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of section 102(1); or  (b) represents directly to the consumer that the goods or services are goods or services to which such a warranty against defects relates. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b0f06e23daa59b0d1b84cd6d8b3e2b8148e85311cd833229210417857bceff97" ;
    cof:pageNumber "292"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-192-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-192-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
