concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-193 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "193 Repairers must comply with prescribed requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-193 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person accepts from another person goods that the other person acquired as a consumer; and  (b) the goods are accepted for the purpose of repairing them; and  (c) the person does not give to the other person a notice that complies with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of section 103(1). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 4-3  Section 194  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person accepts from another person goods that the other person acquired as a consumer; and  (b) the goods are accepted for the purpose of repairing them; and  (c) the person does not give to the other person a notice that complies with the requirements prescribed for the purposes of section 103(1). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 4-3  Section 194  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "84483a82918e5a0231e94a55e6ebe2abe0b4471530ba5c55ee694e64ede7d8b8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "292"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-193-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-193-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
