concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-196 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "196 Requirement to nominate a safety standard"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-196 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person refuses or fails to comply with a request given to the person under subsection 108(2). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$22,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$4,400.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person refuses or fails to comply with a request given to the person under subsection 108(2). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$22,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$4,400.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 4  Offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dc041ced8b47b6323a2e531d03e82a881ca7cd298d1e6cdd47b4a93138a690d5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "295"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-196-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-196-ss-2 ;
