concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "197 Supplying etc. consumer goods covered by a ban"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-197 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, supplies consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) either:  (i) an interim ban on goods of that kind is in force in the place where the supply occurs; or  (ii) a permanent ban on goods of that kind is in force.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, offers for supply (other than for export) consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) the supply would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in or for the purposes of trade or commerce, manufactures, possesses or has control of consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) supply of the goods would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (4) Subsection (3) does not apply if the person does not manufacture, possess or control the goods for the purpose of supplying the goods (other than for export).  (5) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person exports consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) supply of the goods would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (6) Subsection (5) does not apply if the Commonwealth Minister has, by written notice given to the person, approved the export of the goods under section 118(5).  (7) Subsections (1), (2), (3) and (5) are offences of strict liability.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 4-3  Section 198  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Penalty  (8) An offence against subsection (1), (2), (3) or (5) committed by a body corporate is punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater of the following:  (a) $100,000,000;  (b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the body corporate, and any body corporate related to the body corporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3 times the value of that benefit;  (c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—30% of the body corporate’s adjusted turnover during the breach turnover period for the offence.  (9) An offence against subsection (1), (2), (3) or (5) committed by a person other than a body corporate is punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than $2,500,000." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, supplies consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) either:  (i) an interim ban on goods of that kind is in force in the place where the supply occurs; or  (ii) a permanent ban on goods of that kind is in force.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, offers for supply (other than for export) consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) the supply would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in or for the purposes of trade or commerce, manufactures, possesses or has control of consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) supply of the goods would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (4) Subsection (3) does not apply if the person does not manufacture, possess or control the goods for the purpose of supplying the goods (other than for export).  (5) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person exports consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) supply of the goods would be prohibited by subsection (1).  (6) Subsection (5) does not apply if the Commonwealth Minister has, by written notice given to the person, approved the export of the goods under section 118(5).  (7) Subsections (1), (2), (3) and (5) are offences of strict liability.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Offences  Chapter 4 Offences relating to safety of consumer goods and product related services  Part 4-3  Section 198  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Penalty  (8) An offence against subsection (1), (2), (3) or (5) committed by a body corporate is punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater of the following:  (a) $100,000,000;  (b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the body corporate, and any body corporate related to the body corporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3 times the value o"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "125e39bfb6d7c1b9b6fe8483e7d1e3aeae534e6be4250b4266848f9fc3e18fea" ;
    cof:pageNumber "296"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-7 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-8 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-197-ss-9 ;
