doc:sch-2-sec-207-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "207(2) Reasonable mistake of fact" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information relied upon by the defendant that was supplied to the defendant by another person who was, at the time when the contravention occurred:  (a) an employee or agent of the defendant; or  (b) if the defendant is a body corporate—a director, employee or agent of the defendant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "309"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-207-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "207(3) Reasonable mistake of fact"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-207-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If a defence provided by subsection (1) involves an allegation that a contravention was due to reliance on information supplied by another person, the defendant is not entitled to rely on that defence unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice giving such information as the defendant then had that would identify or assist in identifying the other person. 208  Act or default of another person etc." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If a defence provided by subsection (1) involves an allegation that a contravention was due to reliance on information supplied by another person, the defendant is not entitled to rely on that defence unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice giving such information as the defendant then had that would identify or assist in identifying the other person. 208  Act or default of another person etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d93e9c4359cc6808839b7902c1c7faf3c259d591906a45a08c0112f03d28aed3" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-207 ;
    cof:pageNumber "309"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defendant must provide notice to the person who instituted the proceeding within 7 days before the hearing commences." ;
