doc:sch-2-sec-225-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "225(4) Pecuniary penalties and offences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Evidence of information given, or evidence of the production of documents, by an individual is not admissible in criminal proceedings against the individual if:  (a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the documents in proceedings for an order under section 224 against the individual in relation to a consumer protection breach (whether or not the order was made); and  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    cof:pageNumber "327"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-226 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "226 Defence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-226 ;
    values:originalText "If, in proceedings under section 224 against a person other than a body corporate, it appears to a court that the person has, or may have:  (a) engaged in conduct in contravention of a provision referred to in subsection (1)(a) of that section; or  (b) engaged in conduct referred to in subsection (1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of that section that relates to a contravention of such a provision; but that the person acted honestly and reasonably and, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, ought fairly to be excused, the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from liability to a pecuniary penalty under that section." ;
    skos:definition "If, in proceedings under section 224 against a person other than a body corporate, it appears to a court that the person has, or may have:  (a) engaged in conduct in contravention of a provision referred to in subsection (1)(a) of that section; or  (b) engaged in conduct referred to in subsection (1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of that section that relates to a contravention of such a provision; but that the person acted honestly and reasonably and, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, ought fairly to be excused, the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from liability to a pecuniary penalty under that section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3b0f65cd784668771d8a51a0a628fb21efda43ebfceb529c86b08593865d1e68" ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may relieve person from liability to pecuniary penalty if they acted honestly and reasonably." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.328" ;
