ng a person to do any of the following:  (a) refund money;  (b) transfer property;  (c) honour a promise;  (d) destroy or dispose of goods.  (7) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) requiring a person to do an act or thing may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do that act or thing; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to do that act or thing; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person refuses or fails to do that act or thing." ;
