concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-232-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "232(7) Injunctions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-232-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) requiring a person to do an act or thing may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do that act or thing; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to do that act or thing; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person refuses or fails to do that act or thing." ;
    skos:definition "(7) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) requiring a person to do an act or thing may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do that act or thing; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to do that act or thing; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person refuses or fails to do that act or thing."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "694403e9a2e1407646f4334fb77642557de507f440f82b301ce6b7af03761170" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-232 ;
    cof:pageNumber "330"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court power to grant injunction regardless of person's intentions or previous actions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
