doc:sch-2-sec-239 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "239 Orders to redress etc. loss or damage suffered by non-parties" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person:  (i) engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) in contravention of a provision of Chapter 2, Part 3-1," ;
    cof:pageNumber "335"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "240 Determining whether to make a redress order etc. for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-240 ;
    values:originalText "non-parties  (1) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1) against a person referred to in section 239(2)(a), the court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct, since the contravention occurred.  (2) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1) against a person referred to in section 239(2)(b), the court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-parties in relation to the declared term, since the declaration was made.  (3) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1), the court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 241  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct or declared term;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. 241  When a non-party is bound by a redress order etc.  (1) A non-party is bound by an order made under section 239(1) against a person if:  (a) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party in relation to the contravening conduct, or the declared term, to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (b) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction.  (2) Any other order made under section 239(1) that relates to that loss or damage has no effect in relation to the non-party.  (3) Despite any other provision of:  (a) this Schedule; or  (b) any other law of the Commonwealth, or a State or a Territory; no claim, action or demand may be made or taken against the person by the non-party in relation to that loss or damage." ;
    skos:definition "non-parties  (1) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1) against a person referred to in section 239(2)(a), the court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct, since the contravention occurred.  (2) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1) against a person referred to in section 239(2)(b), the court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-parties in relation to the declared term, since the declaration was made.  (3) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1), the court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 241  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct or declared term;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. 241  When a non-party is bound by a redress order etc.  (1) A non-party is bound by an order made under section 239(1) against a person if:  (a) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party in relation to the contravening conduct, or the declared term, to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (b) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction.  (2) Any other order made under section 239(1) that relates to that loss or damage has no effect in relation to the non-party.  (3) Despite any other provision of:  (a) this Schedule; or  (b) any other law of the Commonwealth, or a State or a Territory; no claim, action or demand may be made or taken against the person by the non-party in relation to that loss or damage."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "43ec2c010ec83f5c97f302e2a6b36474f8394ab9d26f45566cb5841cde02034b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "336"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240-ss-2 ;
