    cof:title "240(2) Determining whether to make a redress order etc. for" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1) against a person referred to in section 239(2)(b), the court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-parties in relation to the declared term, since the declaration was made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "336"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "240(3) Determining whether to make a redress order etc. for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-240-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1), the court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 241  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct or declared term;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. 241  When a non-party is bound by a redress order etc." ;
    skos:definition "(3) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1), the court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 241  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct or declared term;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. 241  When a non-party is bound by a redress order etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8cbb6efaf137b513cd39d1dfddf176cd35f4f3e61c11f305493c4639493c4400" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240 ;
    cof:pageNumber "336"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court does not need to make a finding about non-parties in relation to contravening conduct or declared term. No claim or action can be made against the non-party in relation to a loss or damage." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
