doc:sch-2-sec-240-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "240(3) Determining whether to make a redress order etc. for" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In determining whether to make an order under section 239(1), the court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 241  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct or declared term;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. 241  When a non-party is bound by a redress order etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "336"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "240(1) Determining whether to make a redress order etc. for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-240-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A non-party is bound by an order made under section 239(1) against a person if:  (a) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party in relation to the contravening conduct, or the declared term, to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (b) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A non-party is bound by an order made under section 239(1) against a person if:  (a) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party in relation to the contravening conduct, or the declared term, to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (b) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6d2fe5fd8353694ceea6f0354f40b73fb7f348fede57a1631cf3f059141c0ec6" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240 ;
    cof:pageNumber "336"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may consider conduct of person and non-parties in relation to contravention when determining whether to make an order. Non-party bound by order made under section 239(1)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.336" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-240-ss-1-norm .
