concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-243a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "243A(2) Orders made in favour of party to contract containing unfair"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-243a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the orders that a court may make against the respondent include all or any of the following:  (a) an order declaring the whole or any part of the contract, or of a collateral arrangement relating to the contract:  (i) to be void; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or void at all times on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (b) an order:  (i) varying the contract, or such a collateral arrangement, as specified in the order; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—declaring the contract or arrangement to have had effect as so varied on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (c) an order refusing to enforce any or all of the provisions of the contract, or of such a collateral arrangement.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the orders that a court may make against the respondent include all or any of the following:  (a) an order declaring the whole or any part of the contract, or of a collateral arrangement relating to the contract:  (i) to be void; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or void at all times on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (b) an order:  (i) varying the contract, or such a collateral arrangement, as specified in the order; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—declaring the contract or arrangement to have had effect as so varied on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (c) an order refusing to enforce any or all of the provisions of the contract, or of such a collateral arrangement.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5dc958f8fec890af303e2b604a7cb0985806f993b8d57aaea527c948ad76dbcc" ;
