    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the orders that a court may make against the respondent include all or any of the following:  (a) an injunction restraining the respondent from making any future contract that is of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(a) and includes a similar term;  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 245  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) an injunction restraining the respondent from applying or relying on a similar term of any existing contract that is of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(b);  (c) an order declaring the whole or any part of any existing contract of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(b), or of a collateral arrangement relating to such a contract:  (i) to be void; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or void at all times on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (d) an order:  (i) varying such an existing contract, or such a collateral arrangement, as specified in the order; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—declaring the contract or arrangement to have had effect as so varied on and after such date as is specified in the order (which may be a date that is before the date on which the order is made);  (e) an order refusing to enforce any or all of the provisions of such an existing contract, or of such a collateral arrangement." ;
