concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-248 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "248 Order disqualifying a person from managing corporations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-248 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A court may, on application of the regulator, make an order disqualifying a person from managing corporations for a period that the court considers appropriate if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the person has contravened, has attempted to contravene or has been involved in a contravention of any of the following provisions:  (i) a provision of Part 2-2 (which is about unconscionable conduct);  (ia) a provision of Part 2-3 (which is about unfair contract terms);  (ii) a provision of Part 3-1 (which is about unfair practices);  (iii) a provision (other than section 85) of Division 2 of" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A court may, on application of the regulator, make an order disqualifying a person from managing corporations for a period that the court considers appropriate if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the person has contravened, has attempted to contravene or has been involved in a contravention of any of the following provisions:  (i) a provision of Part 2-2 (which is about unconscionable conduct);  (ia) a provision of Part 2-3 (which is about unfair contract terms);  (ii) a provision of Part 3-1 (which is about unfair practices);  (iii) a provision (other than section 85) of Division 2 of"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "96ea5189eae20ce250bf0cc4c3a1ba4d25595614b7024a24cd41a20e19ff9f6d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "345"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may disqualify a person from managing corporations for a period." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
