    cof:title "249(1) Privilege against exposure to penalty or forfeiture—" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In a civil or criminal proceeding under, or arising out of, this Schedule, a person is not entitled to refuse or fail to comply with a requirement:  (a) to answer a question or give information; or  (b) to produce a document or any other thing; or  (c) to do any other act; on the ground that the answer or information, production of the document or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may be, might tend to expose the person to a penalty (including forfeiture) by way of an order under section 248." ;
    cof:pageNumber "346"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-249-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "249(2) Privilege against exposure to penalty or forfeiture—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-249-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person is a defendant in the proceeding or in any other proceeding.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 250  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person is a defendant in the proceeding or in any other proceeding.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 250  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "054b17a527c55034cd2291c96814403078e72759e736fe443703a1178910d9cd" ;
