doc:sch-2-sec-252-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "252(2) Supplying consumer goods for the purpose of re-supply" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) In the proceeding, it is a defence if the defendant proves that:  (a) the consumer goods were acquired by the defendant for the purpose of re-supply; and  (b) the consumer goods were so acquired from a person who carried on in Australia a business of supplying such goods otherwise than as the agent of a person outside Australia; and  (c) either:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies  Part 5-2  Section 253  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (i) the defendant did not know, and could not with reasonable diligence have ascertained, that the consumer goods did not comply with that safety standard, or that the defendant had not complied with that information standard, as the case may be; or  (ii) the defendant relied in good faith on a representation by the person from whom the defendant acquired the goods that there was no safety standard or information standard, as the case may be, for such consumer goods." ;
    cof:pageNumber "348"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-252-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "252(3) Supplying consumer goods for the purpose of re-supply"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-252-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A defendant is not entitled to rely on the defence provided by subsection (2) unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice identifying the person from whom the defendant acquired the consumer goods." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A defendant is not entitled to rely on the defence provided by subsection (2) unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice identifying the person from whom the defendant acquired the consumer goods."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5556298ad15a90b4455a0f6d5a241ef2819bb257b1de122ca139072567f188e8" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-252 ;
    cof:pageNumber "348"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defendant may rely on defence unless court gives leave or defendant provides notice." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
