doc:sch-2-sec-259-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "259(7) Action against suppliers of goods" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) The consumer may take action under this section whether or not the goods are in their original packaging. 260  When a failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure" ;
    cof:pageNumber "354"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-259-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "259(1) Action against suppliers of goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-259-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 259(1)(b) that applies to a supply of goods is a major failure if:  (a) the goods would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the goods depart in one or more significant respects:  (i) if they were supplied by description—from that description; or  (ii) if they were supplied by reference to a sample or demonstration model—from that sample or demonstration model; or  (c) the goods are substantially unfit for a purpose for which goods of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 259(1)(b) that applies to a supply of goods is a major failure if:  (a) the goods would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the goods depart in one or more significant respects:  (i) if they were supplied by description—from that description; or  (ii) if they were supplied by reference to a sample or demonstration model—from that sample or demonstration model; or  (c) the goods are substantially unfit for a purpose for which goods of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "36f9572347ee05e95da457a2eb242e081c9d531e5e534d09ffceda4a0455cfd4" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-259 ;
    cof:pageNumber "354"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure if certain conditions are met. Action against suppliers of goods if guarantee not complied with" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.354" ;
