concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-267-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "267(1) Action against suppliers of services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-267-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 267(1)(b) that applies to a supply of services is a major failure if:  (a) the services would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the services are substantially unfit for a purpose for which services of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are unfit for a particular purpose for which the services were acquired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier of the services;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 267(1)(b) that applies to a supply of services is a major failure if:  (a) the services would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the services are substantially unfit for a purpose for which services of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are unfit for a particular purpose for which the services were acquired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier of the services;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b39f2318ddf290a703b4f06c920b61743c2297d0e87136a9337eef7dc93128a4" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-267 ;
    cof:pageNumber "360"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure if certain conditions are met. Action against suppliers of services" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
