doc:sch-2-sec-267-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "267(1) Action against suppliers of services" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 267(1)(b) that applies to a supply of services is a major failure if:  (a) the services would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the services are substantially unfit for a purpose for which services of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are unfit for a particular purpose for which the services were acquired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier of the services;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    cof:pageNumber "360"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-269 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "269 Termination of contracts for the supply of services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-269 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if, under section 267, a consumer terminates a contract for the supply of services.  (2) The termination takes effect:  (a) at the time the termination is made known to the supplier of the services (whether by words or by conduct indicating the consumer’s intention to terminate the contract); or  (b) if it is not reasonably practicable to communicate with the supplier of the services—at the time the consumer indicates, by means which are reasonable in the circumstances, his or her intention to terminate the contract.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies relating to guarantees  Part 5-4  Section 270  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (3) The consumer is entitled to recover, by action against the supplier of the services, a refund of:  (a) any money paid by the consumer for the services; and  (b) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration provided by the consumer for the services; to the extent that the consumer has not already consumed the services at the time the termination takes effect." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if, under section 267, a consumer terminates a contract for the supply of services.  (2) The termination takes effect:  (a) at the time the termination is made known to the supplier of the services (whether by words or by conduct indicating the consumer’s intention to terminate the contract); or  (b) if it is not reasonably practicable to communicate with the supplier of the services—at the time the consumer indicates, by means which are reasonable in the circumstances, his or her intention to terminate the contract.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies relating to guarantees  Part 5-4  Section 270  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (3) The consumer is entitled to recover, by action against the supplier of the services, a refund of:  (a) any money paid by the consumer for the services; and  (b) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration provided by the consumer for the services; to the extent that the consumer has not already consumed the services at the time the termination takes effect."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "85cec281200aa073d0756d15e8e211b1c1634150a8dacc040a652d0aa365c4a8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "362"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-269-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-269-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-269-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.362" .
