    skos:definition "(3) The consumer is entitled to recover, by action against the supplier of the services, a refund of:  (a) any money paid by the consumer for the services; and  (b) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration provided by the consumer for the services; to the extent that the consumer has not already consumed the services at the time the termination takes effect."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "757ac78effe6b7032e2de43339bca2b29624cc7c5e25d613457bdb22a9c1707f" ;
