doc:sch-2-sec-271-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "271(2) Action for damages against manufacturers of goods" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the guarantee under section 54 is not complied with only because of:  (a) an act, default or omission of, or any representation made by, any person other than the manufacturer or an employee or agent of the manufacturer; or  (b) a cause independent of human control that occurred after the goods left the control of the manufacturer; or  (c) the fact that the price charged by the supplier was higher than the manufacturer’s recommended retail price, or the average retail price, for the goods." ;
    cof:pageNumber "364"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-271-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "271(3) Action for damages against manufacturers of goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-271-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods by description to a consumer; and  (b) the description was applied to the goods by or on behalf of the manufacturer of the goods, or with express or implied consent of the manufacturer; and  (c) the guarantee under section 56 applies to the supply and it is not complied with; an affected person in relation to the goods may, by action against the manufacturer of the goods, recover damages from the manufacturer.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies relating to guarantees  Part 5-4  Section 272  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods by description to a consumer; and  (b) the description was applied to the goods by or on behalf of the manufacturer of the goods, or with express or implied consent of the manufacturer; and  (c) the guarantee under section 56 applies to the supply and it is not complied with; an affected person in relation to the goods may, by action against the manufacturer of the goods, recover damages from the manufacturer.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Remedies relating to guarantees  Part 5-4  Section 272  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9052443bb42dcbed7a60553330d0acdfcb7db340fd29896f0afec538ceace9de" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-271 ;
    cof:pageNumber "364"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Manufacturer liable for damages if guarantee not complied with" ;
