concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-277 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "277 Representative actions by the regulator"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-277 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulator may, by application, commence an action under this Part on behalf of one or more persons identified in the application who are entitled under this Part to take the action.  (2) The regulator may only make the application if it has obtained the written consent of the person, or each of the persons, on whose behalf the application is being made.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Liability of suppliers and credit providers  Part 5-5  Section 278  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulator may, by application, commence an action under this Part on behalf of one or more persons identified in the application who are entitled under this Part to take the action.  (2) The regulator may only make the application if it has obtained the written consent of the person, or each of the persons, on whose behalf the application is being made.  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Enforcement and remedies  Chapter 5 Liability of suppliers and credit providers  Part 5-5  Section 278  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
