doc:sch-2-sec-278-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "278(2) Liability of suppliers and linked credit providers relating to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A linked credit contract is a contract that a consumer enters into with a linked credit provider of a person (the supplier) for the provision of credit in relation to:  (a) the supply by way of sale, lease, hire or hire-purchase of goods to the consumer by the linked credit provider where the supplier supplies the goods, or causes the goods to be supplied, to the linked credit provider; or  (b) the supply by the supplier of goods or services, or goods and services, to the consumer.  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 5  Enforcement and remedies" ;
    cof:pageNumber "371"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-279 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "279 Action by consumer to recover amount of loss or damage"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-279 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a linked credit provider, and a supplier of the goods or services, are liable under section 278 to a consumer for an amount of loss or damage, the consumer may recover the amount by action in a court of competent jurisdiction.  (2) The consumer must bring the action against the linked credit provider and the supplier jointly.  (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if:  (a) the supplier has been dissolved or the winding up of the supplier has commenced; or  (b) both of the following apply:  (i) in the opinion of the court in which the action is taken, it is not reasonably likely that a judgment obtained against the supplier would be satisfied;  (ii) that court has, on the application of the consumer, declared that that subsection does not apply in relation to the proceedings." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a linked credit provider, and a supplier of the goods or services, are liable under section 278 to a consumer for an amount of loss or damage, the consumer may recover the amount by action in a court of competent jurisdiction.  (2) The consumer must bring the action against the linked credit provider and the supplier jointly.  (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if:  (a) the supplier has been dissolved or the winding up of the supplier has commenced; or  (b) both of the following apply:  (i) in the opinion of the court in which the action is taken, it is not reasonably likely that a judgment obtained against the supplier would be satisfied;  (ii) that court has, on the application of the consumer, declared that that subsection does not apply in relation to the proceedings."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0236042acef6bf3163b77158cf462c3d144d4dc9bda5b058c6ca038335eb6dc4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "372"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-279-ss-1 ;
