    cof:pageNumber "383"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-290a-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "290A(4) Application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-290a-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Despite paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) and subsection (3) of this section, the amendments do not apply to a contract, or a term of a contract, to the extent that the operation of the amendments would result in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph of the Constitution).  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 6  Application and transitional provisions" ;
