doc:sch-2-sec-305-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "305(3) Application of amendments relating to unfair contract terms" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If an existing contract is renewed at or after the relevant commencement, the amendments apply to the contract as renewed, on and from the day (the renewal day) on which the renewal takes effect, in relation to conduct that occurs on or after the renewal day." ;
    cof:pageNumber "390"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-305-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "305(4) Application of amendments relating to unfair contract terms"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-305-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If an existing contract is varied at or after the relevant commencement by varying or adding a term and subsection (3) has not already applied in relation to the contract:  (a) the amendments apply to the term as varied or added, and so apply:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Application and transitional provisions  Chapter 6 Application provision relating to the Treasury Laws Amendment (More Competition, Better Prices) Act 2022  Section 305  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (i) on and from the day (the variation day) on which the variation of the contract takes effect; and  (ii) as if the contract as varied had been made on the variation day; and  (iii) in relation to conduct that occurs on and after the variation day; and  (b) section 23(2A)(e) applies in relation to a person proposing the varied or added term, whether before, at or after the relevant commencement; and  (c) subsection 23(2), and section 27, as in force at and after the relevant commencement, apply to the contract." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If an existing contract is varied at or after the relevant commencement by varying or adding a term and subsection (3) has not already applied in relation to the contract:  (a) the amendments apply to the term as varied or added, and so apply:  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2 Application and transitional provisions  Chapter 6 Application provision relating to the Treasury Laws Amendment (More Competition, Better Prices) Act 2022  Section 305  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (i) on and from the day (the variation day) on which the variation of the contract takes effect; and  (ii) as if the contract as varied had been made on the variation day; and  (iii) in relation to conduct that occurs on and after the variation day; and  (b) section 23(2A)(e) applies in relation to a person proposing the varied or added term, whether before, at or after the relevant commencement; and  (c) subsection 23(2), and section 27, as in force at and after the relevant commencement, apply to the contract."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fc004ffc558b8f41e5516313c13c6d07e37309140f90c84032e14f66a6fa4887" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-305 ;
    cof:pageNumber "390"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Amendments apply to a contract on and from the variation day" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.390" ;
