concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-305-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "305(6) Application of amendments relating to unfair contract terms"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-305-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Despite subsections (3) to (5) of this section, the amendments do not apply to a contract, or a term of a contract, to the extent that the operation of the amendments would result in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph of the Constitution).  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 6  Application and transitional provisions" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Despite subsections (3) to (5) of this section, the amendments do not apply to a contract, or a term of a contract, to the extent that the operation of the amendments would result in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph of the Constitution).  Schedule 2  The Australian Consumer Law Chapter 6  Application and transitional provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d8229a5b32f48d855e7ddeaac3bb92843d9e2287ee5084cf73c57f2c1cb5db7c" ;
